company that specializes in developing advanced robots. Founded in 1992 by Marc Raibert, the company is currently headquartered in Waltham, Massachusetts.</h1>\n<h2>Boston Dynamics is recognized as one of the pioneers in the robotics industry and has achieved major successes such as designing two-legged robots named ATLAS and SpotMini, four-legged robots named BigDog and WildCat, as well as robots with extremely advanced movements and balance like the Cheetah and Handle robots.</h2>\n<h3>Boston Dynamics robots are used for various applications due to their highly advanced capabilities, including exceptional movements and balance, powerful jumping and throwing abilities, and sophisticated artificial intelligence technologies. These applications include military, medical, industrial, and even construction uses. For example, the SpotMini robot is used as a commercial and domestic robot for package delivery and supporting construction operations, while the Atlas robot is used in military applications as an assistant robot for search and rescue missions.</h3>\n<h4>As Boston Dynamics robots feature advanced technology, they are expensive and typically used only for specific applications. However, the specialized team at Boston Dynamics ensures that the robots designed by the company perform at a very high level. The Boston Dynamics engineering team includes mechanical, electrical, and electronics engineers, as well as software and AI specialists who continuously develop new technologies and improve the performance of their robots.</h4>\n<h4>One of the notable features of Boston Dynamics robots is their ability to interact with the environment and respond to environmental changes. For example, the Atlas robot can effectively navigate environmental changes such as snow cover or significant elevation changes using its sensors, and also perform complex movements with high precision.</h4>\n<h4>Ultimately, by designing and producing advanced robots, Boston Dynamics has played a crucial role in the robotics industry and has provided innovative solutions for various applications such as military, medical, industrial, and even domestic uses.</h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n<h2>In addition to the Atlas robot, Boston Dynamics has also designed and produced other robots. Some of these robots include:</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<h5>Spot: A four-legged robot capable of moving in difficult and harsh environments such as mines and oil and gas industries.</h5>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h5>Handle: A robot with arms that can pick up and move objects. This robot is specifically designed for use in industrial environments.</h5>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h5>Pick: A robot with arms that can pick up and place objects. This robot is designed for warehouse and logistics services.</h5>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h5>Ava: A robot designed to support patients and provide healthcare services in medical centers.</h5>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h5>These robots, equipped with advanced technologies such as advanced sensor systems, artificial intelligence, and complex software, perform various tasks with extremely high precision and efficiency. Therefore, these robots can be used in a wide range of applications such as healthcare, industry, military, warehousing, and even domestic services.</h5>\n\n\n\n\n\nsrc=\"/media/Boston-Dynamics-Spot-2.jpg\"Boston-Dynamics-Spot robot\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h2>Spot Robot</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h4></h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n<h4>The Spot robot is a four-legged robot designed and built by Boston Dynamics. This robot uses its four legs for movement and to support electronic devices, sensors, and other equipment. Spot is capable of connecting to Wi-Fi networks to communicate with computers and other devices.</h4>\n<h4>Spot can move in environments that are difficult or unsuitable for humans, such as mines, industrial environments, battlefields, areas of natural disasters, and even space. Due to its small and effective size, Spot can easily be used in enclosed and confined spaces.</h4>\n<h4>Given the high cost of manufacturing the Spot robot, it is primarily designed for industrial and military applications. The price of Spot varies depending on the type of installation, base, and additional equipment, ranging from approximately $75,000 to $100,000. Additionally, Boston Dynamics offers companies the option to lease Spot through some of its service packages.</h4>\n<h4>To build the Spot robot, Boston Dynamics uses advanced technologies such as sensor systems, artificial intelligence, complex software, and sophisticated hardware. By combining all these technologies, Spot can automatically detect obstacles, scan environments, identify objects, navigate complex spaces, and perform many other tasks in various environments, meeting industrial and military needs. Using these technologies, Spot has capabilities such as dynamic and stable movement, detecting and reporting obstacles and preventing collisions with them, the ability to work in harsh and subterranean environments, the ability to move in low-light and low-visibility conditions, and many other features.</h4>\n\n\n\n\n<h4>The Spot robot has increased productivity and reduced costs in many industries and industrial sectors. This robot is used in many applications, including safety inspections, environmental monitoring, quality control, support for production systems, worker assistance, error reduction, and other applications.</h4>\n<h4>Additionally, for military applications, Spot can be used in missions such as detecting and <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d8%b4%d8%a8%da%a9%d9%87-%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%b2%db%8c-%d9%88-%d8%a7%d8%b1%d8%aa%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%b7%d8%a7%d8%aa/\" rel=\"noopener\">reporting</a> on the environment, identifying military objects and equipment, preventing hazards, and searching for assistance in critical situations, as well as many other military tasks.</h4>\n<h4>Finally, the Spot robot is one of the most successful industrial and military four-legged robots in the world. By combining advanced technologies and optimal design, this robot is recognized as one of the best tools for automation and cost reduction in various industries.</h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p> </p>\n<h2>Robot - robot -Handle</h2>\n\n\n\nsrc=\"/media/ربات-Handle.jpg\"Robot - robot -Handle\n\n\n\n<h2> </h2>\n\n\n\n<h4>The Handle robot is an articulated robot developed by Boston Dynamics. This robot can automatically, as well as with human operator control, pick up, carry, and place objects. With its intelligent system, this robot can perceive the environment and be aware of obstacles and objects around it, and use its 360-degree cameras to view the environment and provide information to the operator.</h4>\n<h4>As the Handle robot was developed for industrial applications, its capabilities include high speed and precision, resistance to harsh environmental and industrial conditions, and features for specific applications such as moving boxes, handling light and heavy products, and placing goods on shelves.</h4>\n<h4>Since the Handle robot was developed by Boston Dynamics, the company has not published information about its price. However, due to its capabilities and multiple industrial applications, its price is likely relatively high.</h4>\n<h4>In the manufacturing stages of the Handle robot, the Boston Dynamics engineering team first designed and developed it according to the various needs of industries and multiple applications. Then, the various components of the robot, including the arm, gripper, movement system, cameras, and other parts, were produced and manufactured. After the robot is built, testing and validation are performed to ensure that the robot works correctly and meets user expectations.</h4><h4>The control software for the Handle robot uses the Robot Operating System (ROS) environment. This software is used for motion control and communication with other systems in the industrial environment. A graphical user interface is also used to communicate with operator control systems.</h4>\n<h4>Given the various applications of the Handle robot, it is used in some industries such as food, home appliances, automotive, metal industries, and more. This robot serves as a practical tool to facilitate and increase efficiency and accuracy in production and distribution lines, and is effective in reducing costs and increasing industrial productivity.</h4>\n<h4>In summary, the Handle robot is an industrial robotic arm developed by Boston Dynamics. With capabilities such as high speed and precision, specific features for moving goods and objects, and resistance to harsh industrial conditions, it serves as an effective tool to facilitate work and increase industrial productivity. The exact price of the Handle robot has not been published, but it is likely relatively high due to its capabilities.</h4>\n\n\n\n<h4>Unfortunately, the exact price of the Handle robot has not been published by Boston Dynamics. Considering its capabilities and applications in various industries, its price is likely relatively high. Additionally, the price of the Handle robot may vary due to the customization of projects and different settings for each customer.</h4>\n<h2>Robot Pick</h2>\nsrc=\"/media/Pick-ربات-1024x576.jpg\"Pick robot Boston Dynamics\n<h3>The Pick robot is another industrial robot from Boston Dynamics, developed for handling and moving objects in industrial environments. This robot can automatically perform tasks that humans do, helping to increase productivity in industries.</h3>\n<h4>The Pick robot has a set of features and capabilities that we mention below:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h4>Ability to carry and move objects weighing up to 14 kilograms</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>High precision and speed in moving objects</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Ability to identify and grasp objects automatically using imaging</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Connection to industrial control software such as ROS</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Ability to plan robot movements using simulation environments</h4>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>The Pick robot uses grippers mounted on its body to grasp objects and move them to the desired location. To identify objects, this robot uses imaging and analyzes images to identify objects and command them to move.</h4>\n<h4>The features of the Pick robot include the following:</h4>\n<h4>1. Loading and transporting objects with a maximum weight of 15 kilograms.</h4>\n<h4>2. Ability to identify and pick up objects from high-power environments (for example, in direct sunlight or heavy fog) using multiple cameras and sensors.</h4>\n<h4>3. Ability to identify objects with different shapes, colors, and dimensions and pick them up with high precision.</h4>\n<h4>4. Ability to perform loading and transportation operations automatically using control software and vision systems.</h4>\n<h4>The manufacturing stages of the Pick robot include design and engineering, parts production and assembly, testing and validation, and delivery to the customer.</h4>\n<h4>Regarding the price of the Pick robot, the exact price has not been published by Boston Dynamics. Considering its capabilities and applications in various industries, its price is likely relatively high. Additionally, the price of the Pick robot may vary due to the customization of projects and different settings for each customer. For more information, you can contact Boston Dynamics.</h4>\n<h2>Robot Ava</h2>\nsrc=\"/media/Ava.png\"Robot Ava\n\n\n\n\n<h3>The Ava robot is one of Boston Dynamics' robots designed to support employees in indoor and outdoor corporate environments. This robot uses artificial intelligence and machine vision technology to identify objects, recognize faces, and communicate with users.</h3>\n<h4>The features of the Ava robot include:</h4>\n<h4>1. Ability to recognize faces and voices and communicate with users.</h4>\n<h4>2. Providing information about details and work schedules, such as security information and daily work schedules.</h4>\n<h4>3. Ability to send messages to employees and managers in case of problems in the work environment.</h4>\n<h4>4. Ability to detect and collect information about the work environment.</h4>\n<h4>The manufacturing stages of the Ava robot include design and engineering, parts production and assembly, testing and validation, and delivery to the customer.</h4>\n<h4>Regarding the price of the Ava robot, the exact price has not been published by Boston Dynamics. Considering its capabilities and applications in various industries, its price is likely relatively high. Additionally, the price of the Ava robot may vary due to the customization of projects and different settings for each customer. For more information, you can contact Boston Dynamics.</h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h2>Robot Atlas</h2>\n<p> </p>\nsrc=\"/media/atlasربات-robot-_.jpg\"atlas robot\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h4>The Atlas robot is one of Boston Dynamics' important projects in developing smart and agile robots. This robot is a humanoid robot that, using artificial intelligence, machine vision, advanced control systems, and welding and motor mechanisms, has the capability to perform tasks such as lifting and moving heavy and throwable objects, spraying water, or participating in robotic competitions.</h4>\n<h4>This robot is intended for use in various sectors including distribution centers, warehouses, factories, construction industries, and even military and medical applications.</h4>\n<h4>Given the extensive and professional capabilities of the Atlas robot, its manufacturing and production process is very complex and includes design, development and construction, testing and validation, and production of the final version.</h4>\n<h4>Currently, the exact price of the Atlas robot has not been announced, and because it is considered a research and development project of Boston Dynamics, it is probably not easy to find its exact price. However, due to its advanced technologies and diverse applications, its price is likely very high.</h4>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h4>The Atlas robot has very extensive and professional capabilities that, due to its complexity and size, can be applied in many different industries and sectors.</h4>\n<h4> Some of the capabilities of the Atlas robot include:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<h4>Lifting and moving heavy objects: Using powerful motor and welding mechanisms, the Atlas robot is capable of lifting and moving heavy objects and even throwing them.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>High stability: The Atlas robot has an advanced control system that allows it to move with high stability and maintain its balance.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Movement in difficult conditions: With four free limbs and a suitable strategy for movement in difficult conditions such as snow, soil, and various obstacles, the Atlas robot has the ability to move in harsh conditions.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Machine vision: With its machine vision system, the Atlas robot can detect and process images and uses this feature in robotic competitions.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Presence in various industries: Due to its capabilities, the Atlas robot can be used in various sectors including distribution centers, warehouses, factories, construction industries, and even military and medical applications.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Performing dangerous tasks: With the ability to execute complex movements and precise commands, the Atlas robot is capable of performing dangerous and high-risk tasks.</h4>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h5>Therefore, the Atlas robot is one of the most advanced and powerful robots ever built, developed by Boston Dynamics. In summary, the Atlas robot has numerous capabilities and due to its complexity and size, it can be applied in many different industries and sectors.</h5>\n<h5>Of course, it should be noted that the price of the Atlas robot is very high and is only suitable for specific applications. Also, due to its complexity and the need for high technical expertise to control it, maintenance of the Atlas robot can be very expensive. However, the Atlas robot, with its numerous capabilities, is being utilized in various industries and sectors, including automotive, construction, security and defense.</h5>\n\n\n\n<h3>In conclusion, we review the history of the <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d9%86%d8%b1%d9%85-%d8%a7%d9%81%d8%b2%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d9%87%d8%a7%db%8c-%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%84%db%8c-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%86%da%a9%db%8c-%d9%86%d8%a6%d9%88-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%86%da%a9-%d9%be%db%8c%d8%b4%d8%b1/\" rel=\"noopener\">company</a></h3>\n\n\n\n\n<h4>Boston Dynamics is an American technology company founded in 1992 by famous engineer Rodney Brooks and his colleagues. The company operates in the field of designing and developing advanced robots, and its products are used in many industries.</h4>\n<h4>The company's first robot was the Black Cat, built in 1997. This small robot surprised and amazed many people. Then in 2004, a robot named BigDog was created, which is used for carrying heavy loads and military applications. This robot was very advanced and had the ability to drive on uneven surfaces.</h4>\n<h4>After BigDog, numerous robots were designed and built by Boston Dynamics, including the Atlas robot, Spot robot, Handle robot, and the <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d8%b7%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%ad%db%8c-%d8%b1%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%aa/\" rel=\"noopener\">robot</a> Pick.</h4>\n<h4>Boston Dynamics is currently an independent company and was acquired by <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d9%85%d8%b3%d9%84%d9%87-%da%af%d9%88%da%af%d9%84-%d8%a8%d8%a7-%d8%a7%da%a9%d8%a7%d9%86%d8%aa-%d9%87%d8%a7%db%8c-%d8%af%d9%88%d9%84%d9%88%d9%be%d8%b1%db%8c-%d8%a7%db%8c%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%86%db%8c%d8%a7/\" rel=\"noopener\">Google</a> in 2013. However, after a few years, in 2017, Japanese company SoftBank acquired Boston Dynamics from Google. The company currently operates as a subsidiary of SoftBank and strives to help improve working and living conditions by designing and producing advanced robots.</h4>\n\n<h4>Boston Dynamics was founded by Rodney Brooks in 1992 in the United States. Brooks had previously conducted research in artificial intelligence and robotics at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT), and by establishing Boston Dynamics, he pursued his main goal of research and development in advanced robots using artificial intelligence and robotics technology.</h4>\n<h4>Since then, Boston Dynamics has become one of the world's leading manufacturers of advanced robots. The company's goal is to design and produce robots with greater capabilities to work in complex and dangerous environments.</h4>\n<h4>Research and development at Boston Dynamics continues, and efforts to improve and develop new robots using the latest artificial intelligence, robotics, and advanced control systems technologies are ongoing.</h4>\n\n<h5>Thanks Mehrdad</h5>\n\n\nShort Link:<br />\n<a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/sfqt\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>https://mehrdad.ir/sfqt</strong></a></div><aside aria-label=\"Ready to turn this into a product?\" class=\"mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-violet-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-violet-600/10 to-fuchsia-600/10 p-5 sm:p-6\"><h2 class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-bold leading-snug\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-rocket h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-violet-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09z\"></path><path d=\"m12 15-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.35 22.35 0 0 1-4 2z\"></path><path d=\"M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0\"></path><path d=\"M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5\"></path></svg>Ready to turn this into a product?</h2><p class=\"mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground\">In one AI MVP Sprint I take your idea from first sketch to a live product — in weeks, not months.</p><div class=\"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-2.5 sm:fle